<% content_for :title, "Personal Privacy & Consent — Nyika Village" %>

<main class="mx-auto w-[min(1080px,calc(100%-28px))] py-10">
  <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">Personal Privacy &amp; Consent</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl text-village sm:text-4xl">Your household information is private.</h1>

  <%= render "shared/ui/promise", heading: "Plain-language promise" do %>
    <p>
      Your household record is not a public profile. Registry information is used
      for village records, resident services, community needs analysis and
      relevant programmes. Personal information is not displayed publicly or sold.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%# Everything below is this build's own, and is kept because it is specific
      and checkable rather than a general assurance. %>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render "shared/ui/tile",
               title: "You agree to each use separately",
               body: "There is no single box that signs your family up to everything. Village administration, being contacted, being considered for programmes, payment receipts and partner contact are each agreed to on their own — and any of them can be withdrawn later." %>

    <%= render "shared/ui/tile",
               title: "What we deliberately do not ask for",
               body: "No national ID numbers or copies of identity documents. No health details or income. No claims about who owns which land. An age band rather than a date of birth, and a description of where you live rather than a map reference." %>

    <%= render "shared/ui/tile",
               title: "Nothing changes quietly",
               body: "Every change records who made it, when and why. Records are never deleted — if a household leaves, the record is closed rather than erased, so the history stays checkable. You can ask to see everything held about you and have anything wrong corrected." %>

    <%= render "shared/ui/tile",
               title: "Not everyone at the office sees everything",
               body: "Whoever registers households cannot see who asked for welfare support, and whoever runs support cases cannot see who contributed to a collection. Nobody can join those two together." %>

    <%= render "shared/ui/tile",
               title: "Money is checked, not held",
               body: "The registry never holds your money. You pay to an approved account or an authorised collector, and the office records the receipt. Whoever takes a payment is never the person who confirms it arrived." %>

    <%= render "shared/ui/tile",
               title: "Your PIN is yours",
               body: "The office issues a temporary PIN in person and you replace it with your own. Nobody can set or reset a PIN just by knowing your phone number — which is what stops someone else opening your household." %>
  </div>

  <%= render "shared/ui/notice" do %>
    Something recorded about you that is wrong? Speak to the village office —
    <%= registry_number %>.
  <% end %>
</main>
